<title>SOUTH AFRICA: ATHLETICS-JAMAICA'S OTTEY TO RUN IN SOUTH AFRICA.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-JAMAICA'S OTTEY TO RUN IN SOUTH AFRICA.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jamaican sprint queen Merlene Ottey will race in South Africa this summer, Athletics South Africa (ASA) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Ottey, the silver medalist in both 100 and 200 metres at the Atlanta Olympics, will compete in three meetings across South Africa from the end of this month. She will race in Pietersburg on March 27, Pretoria on April 2 and Cape Town on April 8.</p>
</text>
